U-Boot for the Ronetix RNX-iMX93-OSM and RNX-iMX93-SMARC boards

Supported boards
================
  defconfig                     Board             LPDDR4X
  ----------------------------  ----------------  -------
  imx93-rnx_osm_defconfig       RNX-iMX93-OSM     1 GB
  imx93-rnx_smarc_defconfig     RNX-iMX93-SMARC   1 GB
  imx93-rnx_smarc_2gb_defconfig RNX-iMX93-SMARC   2 GB

Common hardware:
  - PMIC:     NXP PCA9451A at 0x25 on LPI2C2
  - Console:  LPUART1, 115200 8N1
  - eMMC:     USDHC1 (U-Boot mmc 0)
  - SD card:  USDHC2 (U-Boot mmc 1)
  - Ethernet: EQOS (eth1, default, PHY address 1), FEC (eth0, PHY address 2)

Quick Start
===========
$ export ARCH=arm64
$ export CROSS_COMPILE=/opt/cross/aarch64-ronetix-linux-gnu-11.1.0/bin/aarch64-ronetix-linux-gnu-
$ make imx93-rnx_osm_defconfig
$ tools/imx_build_firmware.sh imx93
$ make

The result is flash.bin (ELE container, SPL, DDR firmware, BL31 and U-Boot).
Do not use "make flash.bin", on i.MX93 this target fails with
"No rule to make target 'u-boot.cnt'".

CPU revision
============
The ELE container in flash.bin depends on the i.MX93 CPU revision.
The default is A1 (RNX-iMX93-SMARC v1.1). For CPU revision A0
(RNX-iMX93-SMARC v1.0):

$ CPU_REV=A0 tools/imx_build_firmware.sh imx93
$ make

The script copies the container of the selected revision to
mx93-ahab-container.img, which board/ronetix/imx93-osm/imximage.cfg
appends to flash.bin. The U-Boot binary is the same for both revisions.
A flash.bin with the container of the wrong revision does not boot.
Run the script without CPU_REV to go back to A1.

Write flash.bin to the SD card at offset 32 KiB
===============================================
$ sudo dd if=flash.bin of=/dev/sdX bs=1k seek=32 conv=fsync

Note: the offset is 32 KiB on i.MX93, not 33 KiB as on i.MX8MM.

Write flash.bin to the eMMC with uuu
====================================
Set the boot switches to Serial Downloader:

  Boot mode                      1-2    3-4    5-6   7-8
  -----------------------------  -----  -----  ----  ----
  Cortex-A55 Serial Downloader   CLOSE  OPEN   OPEN  OPEN
  Cortex-A55 eMMC                OPEN   CLOSE  OPEN  OPEN

$ uuu -b tools/u-boot.uuu flash.bin

The -b is needed, otherwise uuu ignores the file name. The path of the image is
relative to the current directory. When U-Boot is loaded over USB
it enters "fastboot usb 0" instead of booting. "flash bootloader" writes to
the eMMC boot partition 1, as defined by ${fastboot_raw_partition_bootloader}.

Only the first USB controller (usbotg1) can be used as a USB device. It runs
in the mode selected by its ID pin (dr_mode = "otg"), usbotg2 is host only.
